##========= /etc/anon/anonrc — the BUYER's way onto the Anyone network ======##
#
# A SOCKS5 proxy and nothing else. It publishes no service and relays nothing
# for anyone; it exists so `make smoke-hs` can resolve and dial a `.anyone`
# address the way a real buyer does.
#
# This is what the TOON client's `socksProxy` names, and — because `proxyRpc`
# defaults to true — what its chain RPC rides as well.
#
# Vendored from the anytoon sibling checkout's config/anonrc-client.
#
# NOT PART OF SERVING. The `anon` + `hs-ingress` pair is the ingress; this
# daemon is the client side of the rehearsal and nothing depends on it. It sits
# on its own compose network (`hs-payer`) with NO ROUTE to anvil or to any
# connector: belt to the braces, because a `.anyone` name cannot be resolved by
# anything but the Anyone network, so a packet that arrives at all arrived over
# a circuit. Being unable to reach those containers directly makes the shortcut
# impossible as well as unused.
#
# Mounted READ-ONLY at /etc/anon/anonrc.

# WITHOUT THIS THE DAEMON DOES NOT START — see conf/anonrc.
AgreeToTerms 1

User anond
DataDirectory /var/lib/anon

# EXPLICIT for the same reason as the service daemon's: a read-only mount and an
# entrypoint that would otherwise append one.
Nickname toonsandboxbuyer

# A CLIENT, not a relay: this opens circuits and carries nobody else's.
ClientOnly 1
ORPort 0
DirPort 0
ControlSocket 0

# The one surface. Bound to 0.0.0.0 because compose publishes it to the host's
# loopback, where `make smoke-hs` runs; the policy below is the belt to that
# braces.
SocksPort 0.0.0.0:9050
SocksPolicy accept 10.0.0.0/8
SocksPolicy accept 172.16.0.0/12
SocksPolicy accept 192.168.0.0/16
SocksPolicy accept 127.0.0.0/8
SocksPolicy reject *

Log notice stdout
Log notice file /var/lib/anon/notice.log
